nite with mortal kombat  director paul w  s anderson for his 2008 remake of death  race  he also reprised 14k his character in  death race  for the film's first two sequels death  race 2  and death race inferno portraying jen in  2009 street fighter the legend of chun  li  gave him the rare distinction of playing  both a mortal kombat character  and a street fighter character he also  had a small role in the 2006 film  adaptation of doa  dead or alive giving him the rare  fighting game movie adaptation hat trip  according to a 2020 interview with the  podcast monsters madness and magic  shu has since dedicated himself to  parenting so the  ne the last seven years i've been  basically devoted myself  to um raise my kid lyndon ashby was just  breaking into major motion pictures when  he was cast as hollywood big shock  johnny cage  just before mortal kombat he played  supporting roles opposite kevin costner  and luke perry in wyatt earp  in eight seconds respectively on mortal  kombat ashby enjoyed the freedom to  improvise and influence his  characterization  but he found shooting the fight  sequences to be a punishing experience  unhappy with the role he was offered for  the sequel ashby declined to return for  mortal kombat annihilation after mortal  kombat  he continued to appear in smaller action  films and thrillers throughout the 90s  and 2000s  but his most famous role would come in  2011  when he was cast as sheriff noah  stalinski in mtv's tv remake of teen  wolf  playing the father of one of the lead  characters ashby appeared in 88 episodes  of the hit series  all these years later however ashby  hasn't forgotten his video game days  in 2020 he recorded new voice lines and  lent his likeness to the quote  hollywood combatant skin for johnny cage  and mortal kombat 11.  kerry hiroyuki tagawa is one of those  great recognizable actors  he appeared in action films like  showdown in little tokyo  and rising sun before becoming the  villainous shang tsung in mortal kombat  while only making a brief appearance in  mortal kombat annihilation  tagawa is the one original actor to  reprise a role in the web series mortal  kombat legacy appearing in three  episodes in 2013.  he also returned to shangsung in 2019's  mortal kombat 11  as the game's canonical version of shang  tsung he is however succeeded by chen  han  in the 2021 mortal kombat film outside  of mortal kombat  tagawa has remained a constant on-screen  presence  he had a recurring role on the netflix  reboot of lost in space  and he portrayed trade minister nobusuke  tagomi  on three seasons of amazon's the man in  the high castle  tagawa has voiced frustrations over the  limited roles available to asian actors  in hollywood which has led to his long  tenure playing villains  in a 2006 documentary titled the slanted  screen  tagawa said if i'm going to choose  between a wimpy businessman and a bad  guy  i'm gonna play a bad guy because i got  balls  bridget wilson had one heck of a 1995  only two years into an exciting film  career that began opposite arnold  schwarzenegger in last action hero  wilson ended up starring in two hit  movies in one year  first she appeared as third grade  teacher veronica vaughn  in adam sandler's billy madison next she  would win the role of special forces  officer sonja blade in mortal kombat  which became available  after cameron diaz hot off her comedy  debut in the mask  broke her risk training for the film  wilson continued to appear in multiple  movies a year  including four feature films in 1997  which left no room in her schedule for  mortal kombat annihilation  or so she claimed however wilson would  return to voice the classic  mk movie sonia blade skin for mortal  kombat 11.  since 2008 wilson has withdrawn from the  busy life of a hollywood actor to pursue  another of her lifelong dreams  being a full-time parent and homemaker  following a prosperous modeling career  brooklyn actress talisa soto  already had a prominent role in the  blockbuster action film licensed to kill  before becoming outworlds princess  katana in mortal kombat  after the video game adaptation soto  found herself cast in a string of  infamously bad films  such as mortal kombat annihilation the  direct-to-video adaptation of the pulpy  horror comic vampirella  in 2002's ballistic x versus sever  since then she made one more credited  acting appearance in 2009 with remission  written and directed by her  brother-in-law peter bratt  soto has been out of public life for  over a decade and has given few  interviews  but she can often be seen walking the  red carpet at premieres and award shows  with her husband  actor benjamin bratt with whom she has  two children  in the mortal kombat movie english actor  trevor goddard portrayed the smirking  mercenary kano with an australian accent  that was later adopted in the game  series  so what's the origin behind that voice  well goddard spent years in hollywood  claiming to have been a boxer from perth  australia  which was according to the lakeland  ledger a total invention  those rare interviews with goddard that  can be found online still cling to this  fiction  leaving very little information behind  about his real life  while his film career never took off  goddard found a home on the cbs drama  jag  as lieutenant commander mike brumby he  appeared in 42 episodes of the series  alongside his friend catherine bell whom  he met on the set of the low budget  action film men of war in 1994.  sadly goddard died in 2003 at the age of  40 from a drug overdose  his final feature film roll which hit  screens a month later was grapple  a pirate aboard the titular vessel and  pirates of the caribbean the curse of  the black pearl  one of the most iconic characters from  the mortal kombat video game series  scorpion had a minor role in the  original film where he was all but  silent  save for his famous taunt get over here  since his only purpose in the film was  to fight the role was filmed by stunt  actor chris casamassa who also doubled  as the onset trainer for his on-screen  opponent  johnny cage actor lyndon ashby casamassa  reprised scorpion in mortal kombat  annihilation and in four episodes of the  short-lived syndicated television series  mortal kombat conquest  other highlights of his stunned career  include doubling as the caped crusader  for george clooney in 1997's batman and  robin  and coordinating on blade the following  year he is now  president and ceo of red dragon karate a  school founded in 1965 by his father  louis d casamassa he is also the head  instructor at the glendora california  location  the man under sub-zero's mask was french  martial artist  dancer and personal trainer francois  petit petit was involved in the film  long before the rest of the cast  working to recruit more stunned  performers when a suitable actor  couldn't be found to play sub-zero  the role fell to petit though his on-set  responsibilities led to a reduction of  the part  in addition to his work staging the  action petit was also kari hiroyuki  tagawa's fight trainer  petit has personally trained huge stars  throughout his career  including arnold schwarzenegger and  dwayne johnson he served on the wwf  medical staff in the 90s and can be seen  tending to mick foley after the  wrestler's now famous 16-foot fall in  the quote  hell in the cell match had 1998's king  of the ring event  while no longer active in hollywood  petite has worked as a dance  choreographer consultant as recently as  2020.  master keith cook hirobayashi was  already a celebrated martial arts  competitor before he began taking roles  in hollywood action movies  in 1990 he appeared opposite martial  arts legend cynthia rothrock  in the two back-to-back films chyna  o'brien and chyna o'brien too  after initial test screenings for mortal  kombat came back with one prevailing  request  quote more fights cook was brought in to  participate in one of the added action  sequences  as reptile cook's decades of experience  made him a great dance partner for rob  and shoes lou kay  cook was invited back in 1997 for a  fighting and speaking role as the new  sub-zero in mortal kombat annihilation  and he would also join robin shu in  beverly hills ninja that same year  while he no longer appears in films he  is the owner and head instructor of  keith cook  studios in brentwood california where  he's trained several hollywood stars in  preparation for athletically demanding  roles  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  mortal kombat are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  you
 

